  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building support to CCFN (Caritas Norway project)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CCFN has a large Caritas Norway funded project, focussing on emergency livelihoods in NE Nigeria. 

As part of this project, CAFOD will provide some capacity development support to CCFN. Following a consultation process, CCFN identified that their greatest humanitarian capacity development need was logistics. 

In February 2018, CAFOD will facilitate a self assessment and deliver a 5 days logistics training for CCFN. This process will use the standards and materials developed by the Partner Capacity Enhancement in Logistics (PARCEL) Project http://parcelproject.org/about-the-parcel-project/ which covers the following topics:

1. Asset management; 
2. Procurement; 
3. Warehousing; 
4. Fleet Management; 
5. Distribution; 
6. Cross Cutting (security etc). 

A follow up visit will take place in late March 2018 to check progress against the action plan and identify any outstanding tasks.</narrative>
  </description>
